==Old English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|ang|þenċean}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*þankijaną}}. Cognate with {{etyl|ofs|-}} {{m|ofs|thenka}} ({{etyl|fy|-}} {{m|fy|tinke}}), {{etyl|osx|-}} {{m|osx|thenkian}} ({{etyl|nds|-}} {{m|nds|denken}}), {{etyl|odt|-}} {{m|odt|thenken}} ({{etyl|nl|-}} {{m|nl|denken}}), {{etyl|goh|-}} {{m|goh|thenken}} ({{etyl|de|-}} {{m|de|denken}}), {{etyl|non|-}} {{m|non|þekkja}} ({{etyl|gmq-osw|-}} {{m|gmq-osw|þækkia}}, {{etyl|is|-}} {{m|is|þekkja}}), {{etyl|got|-}} {{m|got|𐌸𐌰𐌲𐌺𐌾𐌰𐌽}}. All ultimately from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{m|ine-pro|*teng-||to think}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈθent͡ʃan/|lang=ang}}

===Verb===
{{ang-verb|head=þenċan}}

# to [[think]]

